implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (RED). Edit scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs only (Edit tool), the one suite that postflight.sh and postflight.ps1 both run.

Add `async function wtSerenaYml()` right after wtCompletion, where REVIEW and mainOf are defined. Register it as 'wt-serena-yml':wtSerenaYml next to 'wt-completion':wtCompletion in the Object.assign(cases,{...}) block. Do not touch that block's last line: WT-14 (task-befdddf7, WORKING) edits these same files, so keep the hunks small.

The case is a project that TRACKS .serena/project.yml:
- `p=repo('wt-serena-yml',{settings:LANDS})`, `f='.serena/project.yml'`, `yml='project_name: fixture\nlanguages: [x]\n'`;
- `write(path.join(p.dir,f),yml); git(p.top,'add','--',f); git(p.top,'commit','-qm','track project.yml'); git(p.top,'update-ref','refs/heads/main','HEAD')`, so main and moe/control both track it and the control is clean;
- `main=mainOf(p)`.

Run 1, a checkpoint: `landRun(p,'wt-serena-yml-1',{'src/a.txt':'task a\n'})`, `head=revOf(p.top,p.branch)`. Assert:
- r.code 0 and head !== main;
- the premise: W holds WT-06's copy, `readOr(path.join(p.W,f))==='project_name: "fixture@'+TASK+'"\nlanguages: [x]\n'` (a plain scalar is re-quoted with JSON.stringify), and `git(p.W,'status','--porcelain','--',f)` matches /^ M /;
- `git(p.top,'show',head+':'+f)===yml` (message: 'the checkpoint carried the WT-06 copy to the task branch'), and src/a.txt landed;
- the log matches /MOE_ATTR_EXCLUDED/.

Run 2, a completion: `landRun(p,'wt-serena-yml-2',{'src/a.txt':'done\n'},REVIEW)`, `c=mainOf(p)`. Assert r.code 0, c !== main, and `[git(p.top,'show',c+':'+f), git(p.top,'show',c+':src/a.txt')]` deep-equals [yml,'done\n'] (message: 'the completion carried the WT-06 copy to the target').

RED run (sh engine), from the worktree root in WSL bash. The launcher harnesses may run in place, and they run from a task worktree since task-3c4be125 and task-86431c31:
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" && T=$(mktemp -d) && cp scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js "$T/" && env -u MOE_SESSION_ID -u MOE_ATTEMPT_ID -u MOE_ATTEMPT_GENERATION MOE_WORKTREE_ONLY=wt-serena-yml node scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs sh "$PWD/scripts/moe-agent.sh" "$T/postflight-fake-proxy.js" "$T" "$(command -v bash)"

Expected: `[worktree] wt-serena-yml FAILED: AssertionError ...the checkpoint carried the WT-06 copy to the task branch`, i.e. the renamed name landed, which is the defect observed. Save that line for the complete_task summary.
error handling: a TypeError or a failure before that assertion is a harness problem (mem:gotcha-postflight-worktree-mutant-copy), not RED. Fix the case until it fails exactly there.
